{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic","id":111399,"title":"Dragon-Blooded vs Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-12T05:06:52-07:00","id":111399,"title":"Dragon-Blooded vs Magic","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/Untitled-5.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> So we all know that Manuel: DB don't rank exactly high when it come to quality, but I'm curious on what people think about the Dragon-Blooded's weakness when it come to magic. I'm talking about some of their charms that outright fail when opposes to action that are enhanced by magic or make by Celestial Exalted. Now while I'm aware that Dragon-Blooded are just mere Terrestrial but &quot;vs Magic = Fail&quot; is such a boring way to enforce that, and the excuse of &quot;DB + Teamwork = Really Strong DB, guy !&quot; is kinda silly when:<br /> <br /> 1/ The Cooperative keyword require you to know the same charm, except that people don't generally like to buy charms possesses by other PC.<br /> 2/ Not sure what people think about Terrestrial (Ability) Reinforcement, but I think just touching someone and grant them ability dots is kinda......boring mechanically.<br /> 3/ Charms that don't fall in problem 1 and 2 have high Essence requirement and a shit load of preg charm instead :look at With One Mind:<br /> <br /> So yeah, your opinion about the idea that Dragon-Blooded can't even compare to street urchin because street urchin may get a Celestial Exaltation one day and every DB loosing again someone with an Excellency, go !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-12-2014, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T05:09:33-07:00","id":111402,"title":"","content":"It's irritating, runs counter to the fluff, and disincentivizes playing a DB. In games I've been in, we ignore that rule in favor of the more general rule that when magic meets magic, whoever's got a better dice pool wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T05:15:57-07:00","id":111405,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who is a diehard Solar fan? I thought it was stupid, a middle finger to a sizable part of the fandom, un-fun and I'm really glad Dragon-Blooded are going to get treated with more respect in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T06:09:30-07:00","id":111430,"title":"","content":"It's stupid, everyone knows it's stupid, and considering that the Devs have said they want to flatten the power curve slightly, I expect it to die in a fire in 3rd ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:10:32-07:00","id":111445,"title":"","content":"On that note, anyone who ever says &quot;mere Terrestrial&quot; again, let alone puts the phrase in print in 3E: I am going to <i>cut you</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T07:51:20-07:00","id":111470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111445#post111445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, anyone who ever says &quot;mere Terrestrial&quot; again, let alone puts the phrase in print in 3E: I am going to <i>cut you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds you that for all it's faults Scroll of Heroes at least respected Heroic Mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:29:21-07:00","id":111505,"title":"","content":"Something I would like to see would be that if a group of DB preforms a spell together then they can go up a circle. circle ritual spell casting.<br /> <br /> Maybe each members need a ladder to arcane charm and then a select group can buy a 2nd circle spell which they can only perform if there a more than 2 people casting the spell.<br /> <br /> would make for some nice heptagram study groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:41:31-07:00","id":111511,"title":"","content":"Man, that opening picture makes me chuckle. I can tell what it's meant to convey, but... listen, lady? That's Mnemon you're dealing with (I think.) A massively powerful sorcerer, mistress of dozens or even hundreds of bound demons, and lest we forget, a freaking centuries old Dragon-Blood. <br /> <br /> And you are turning your back on her, apparently confident in the idea that some bruises and a few knives through her clothing are enough to signal victory. For pity's sake, none of them are even through anything more critical than her silk! <br /> <br /> Likewise, some of the other anti-Terrestrial things you find in the books are so ridiculous they're almost funny. Like that bit in Compass Yu-Shan, which appears to be under the impression that a celestial deity could speak to a Dragon-Blooded as though they happen to be a lost pet without fear of retribution. And not, you know, get reminded of the importance of manners by a group that boasts several thousand Exalted specifically trained in kicking the backsides of disrespectful gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1354-grey-seer","name":"Grey Seer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:41:42-07:00","id":111512,"title":"","content":"Let me play a bit of devils advocate here. The cooperative charms I can't defend at all, because it's just stupid to need two PCs with the same charm purchases to work together. The only thing I could say is to ask how it could be any other way. The failing against celestials and magic in general, can be okay. Out of play it feels like a big middle finger. In play it forces you to adapt and be clever. If your soak booster doesn't work against demons you need to find another way to stay alive, maybe a plot hook. If your tracking charm fails against anathema then you need to track them other ways, maybe by asking local spirits or investigating the town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:42:32-07:00","id":111513,"title":"","content":"I don't expect to see direct reference to failing against Celestial Exalted in 3e, but DB charms failing against magic (rather than going to roll-off) I expect to stay.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, that with the exception of other Exalts, most beings *don't have access* to broad supernatural effects. (And even if other Exalts have access, that doesn't mean they'll have them.)<br /> <br /> As an example? The DB trackless passage charm? 2/3 of the printed first circle demons *do not have an awareness excellency*. That means they *automatically succeed* against 2/3rds of the supernatural oppponents. (And in the case of the other third, they go to rolloff because the charm specificially says so).<br /> <br /> That's not a weak effect.<br /> <br /> In general, when looking at the DB charms like this, it's important to remember that A) The vast majority of beings don't even have *access* to supernatural power in all fields, and of the ones that have access (other exalts) many of them will still lack it.<br /> <br /> So, unless your ST is a total dick, your supernaturally stealthy DB will be able to be supernaturally stealthy the vast majority of the time, but when faced with a supernatural opponent &quot;designed&quot; to counter that, you'll have to work around that. Presumably it might be someone else in the games time to shine.<br /> <br /> I don't see this being a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":782,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","user":"Lafing Cat","date":". 04-12-2014, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T08:55:56-07:00","id":111519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111513#post111513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's take a look at the DB charms that have clauses about being &quot;Defeated by Magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Soundless Passage Technique:</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of charms that don't work against other charms or sorcery though, but I suspect you already knew that and wanted to be pedantic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:00:15-07:00","id":111522,"title":"","content":"The effects of Dragon-Blooded vs Celestial Magic... or Dragon-Blooded vs higher-Essence magic... I thought was pretty lame. I don't find it interesting inside the setting, and as a player I don't find the extra challenge fun when presented in that manner.<br /> <br /> However, the effects where Dragon-Blooded get more powerful in the presence of a Celestial Anima I DID think was pretty cool. They're magic being reactive to Celestial magic in a positive way is neat, and re-enforces the concept of their original purpose. But doing that in reverse I found to be lackluster and painful. <br /> <br /> It's like in Fairy Tail when <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Jellal gives Natsu the golden flame. His magic unlocked that bit of true potential in Natsu, and made him bad-ass enough to beat down Zero. And it was beautiful. Not sure why I'm spoiling this though...it's a pretty old episode.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:17:39-07:00","id":111533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111519#post111519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plenty of charms that don't work against other charms or sorcery though, but I suspect you already knew that and wanted to be pedantic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I accidently posted that as I was going to go through them all one by one (and was including that for completeness) but then I scrapped that idea in favor of making a more general point.<br /> <br /> I will note that it's not &quot;just&quot; DBs who have charms that fail vs opposing magic. Fair Folk are full of them (a splat that's supposed to be roughly comparable in power) and even Celestials have a few. Alchemicals, Infernals both have charms that protect against &quot;non-magical&quot; attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Areliex</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> or Dragon-Blooded vs higher-Essence magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is by no means limited to DBs, it's *extraordinarily* common. I'm pretty sure every single splat (and all of the NPC types) has some magic that only works vs (equal or) lower essence targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:52:59-07:00","id":111569,"title":"","content":"It's all in the execution. Lets go to your point about Fair Folk and Dragon-Blooded being comparable in power.<br /> <br /> Bastion of the Self (Sword) is a Raksha saying &quot;I'm not going to die to some stupid mortal&quot; unless they come at her with iron weapons she'll laugh them off. If she fights an essence user she gets at least +2 DV.<br /> <br /> Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode is a Dragon-Blooded saying a very similar thing, but she gets an instant charm that costs 3m 1wp a time and can still get taken out by an unexpected attack (which lets be reasonable, is something that mortals fighting a superior opponent are going to try and do). If she fights an essence user then she needs the next charm along because this one won't help her.<br /> <br /> I know who feels by far the most powerful to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:56:13-07:00","id":111574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111569#post111569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all in the execution. Lets go to your point about Fair Folk and Dragon-Blooded being comparable in power.<br /> <br /> Bastion of the Self (Sword) is a Raksha saying &quot;I'm not going to die to some stupid mortal&quot; unless they come at her with iron weapons she'll laugh them off. If she fights an essence user she gets at least +2 DV.<br /> <br /> Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode is a Dragon-Blooded saying a very similar thing, but she gets an instant charm that costs 3m 1wp a time and can still get taken out by an unexpected attack (which lets be reasonable, is something that mortals fighting a superior opponent are going to try and do). If she fights an essence user then she needs the next charm along because this one won't help her.<br /> <br /> I know who feels by far the most powerful to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're comparing apples to oranges here. A Solar with Heavenly Guardian Defense (which costs 8 motes at a time!) (or SSE) can be taken out by an unexpected attack from that same mortal. Are you arguing Fair Folk feel more powerful than Solars to you?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T09:58:58-07:00","id":111576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111574#post111574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're comparing apples to oranges here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Both characters learn a charm because they went &quot;I don't want to die to a mortal&quot; and both characters are at a distinct disadvantage if they suddenly encounter a supernatural. The Fae is better off in both situations. Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode as it exists in MoEP: DB has little value beyond &quot;I don't want to die to mortals&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T10:02:55-07:00","id":111578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111512#post111512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of play it feels like a big middle finger. In play it forces you to adapt and be clever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one pretty much poisons the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T10:06:47-07:00","id":111580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grey Seer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111511#post111511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that opening picture makes me chuckle. I can tell what it's meant to convey, but... listen, lady? That's Mnemon you're dealing with (I think.) A massively powerful sorcerer, mistress of dozens or even hundreds of bound demons, and lest we forget, a freaking centuries old Dragon-Blood.<br /> <br /> And you are turning your back on her, apparently confident in the idea that some bruises and a few knives through her clothing are enough to signal victory. For pity's sake, none of them are even through anything more critical than her silk!<br /> <br /> Likewise, some of the other anti-Terrestrial things you find in the books are so ridiculous they're almost funny. Like that bit in Compass Yu-Shan, which appears to be under the impression that a celestial deity could speak to a Dragon-Blooded as though they happen to be a lost pet without fear of retribution. And not, you know, get reminded of the importance of manners by a group that boasts several thousand Exalted specifically trained in kicking the backsides of disrespectful gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sidebar is one of the single worst things ever written in Second Edition. It directly contradicts so much previously established stuff. And that Infernal is a few seconds away from being <i>absolutely murdered</i> by a team of Second Circle Demon bodyguards after underestimating a &quot;mere Terrestrial&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the topic of DB Charms that fail against magic we completely ignore that text. 2e's Dragon-Blooded Charms are still a mess that was never properly fixed even after <i>Ten Thousand Correct Actions</i> or the 2.5 errata, but at least the autofailure crap is easily excised for a small improvement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T11:32:00-07:00","id":111635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111445#post111445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, anyone who ever says &quot;mere Terrestrial&quot; again, let alone puts the phrase in print in 3E: I am going to <i>cut you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can your knife, enhanced by mere Terrestrial charms, penetrate Celestial defenses? I submit that it cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://s67.photobucket.com/user/EggmanSizzle/media/Ex3KSBadge_zps950331e7.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i67.photobucket.com/albums/h311/EggmanSizzle/Ex3KSBadge_zps950331e7.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"http://s67.photobucket.com/user/EggmanSizzle/media/BackerBadgesmall_zps424a0237.png.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i67.photobucket.com/albums/h311/EggmanSizzle/BackerBadgesmall_zps424a0237.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/846-eggmansizzle","name":"eggmansizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar846_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:09:23-07:00","id":111666,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite things is Bloodhound Nose Technique not being content with itself failing against magic (probably because someone had the nerve to only make it fail against magic of people with lower Essence score), so they made it specifically fail against it's natural counter in the Terrestrial arsenal, Trackless Walk Style. Which itself, of course, also fails against tracking magic. It's like, those two Charms fail against magic so hard, they need a kind of bizarro UFvIO rule to determine who fails the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:13:13-07:00","id":111673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111576#post111576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. Both characters learn a charm because they went &quot;I don't want to die to a mortal&quot; and both characters are at a distinct disadvantage if they suddenly encounter a supernatural. The Fae is better off in both situations. Portentous Comet Deflecting Mode as it exists in MoEP: DB has little value beyond &quot;I don't want to die to mortals&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you mean by &quot;better off in both situations&quot;. A Fae can be hit by *any* mortal who stunts. A DB needs a mortal to successfully make an unexpected attack. (Which, they have ways to negate in e.g. awareness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":782,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","user":"Lafing Cat","date":". 04-12-2014, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T12:31:52-07:00","id":111689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111673#post111673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have no idea what you mean by &quot;better off in both situations&quot;. A Fae can be hit by *any* mortal who stunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now see that the errata got that and you're acting like that's what it said in Graceful Wicked Masques. Also PCDM is now 8m 1wp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-12-2014, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T13:57:12-07:00","id":111744,"title":"","content":"I can't remember, is that art in the first post from one of the books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:07:05-07:00","id":111750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111744#post111744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember, is that art in the first post from one of the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>MoEP: Infernals I believe.<br /> It amuses me because I imagine Mnemon and Cyan ran off to join the circus at some point and she's pouting and going &quot;being a knife thrower's assistant was not as fun as previously indicated&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:26:41-07:00","id":111765,"title":"","content":"I can understand the drive behind making many or most modes of Dragon Blooded offense or defense falter in the face of empowered opposition as a (fairly crude, admittedly) way of presenting the idea of them as the weakest Exalted. It's probably eased in by a fairly binary system.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a more granular and nuanced system will have a more natural and satisfying way of presenting that idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T14:32:56-07:00","id":111767,"title":"","content":"I'm not intrinsically against powers that fail to magic, but I will be very disappointed if Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode isn't scourged from 3e, because everything about it is terrible. 2e exacerbated the problem by ensuring that the world was full of lesser supernaturals who could get around it by spending one mote on a combat excellency, but even in 1e it was one of the worst charms in the DB book. Maybe the worst. It's a costly instant effect that only works against minor threats -- I cannot dream of actually taking it except to get to something beyond it.<br /> <br /> In some cases it would be worth making a new &quot;super parry&quot; charm with the same name, but it also has one of the worst charm names in the entire game. At least &quot;Salty Dog Method&quot; kind of sounds stupid in an ironic, jokey way. &quot;Portentous Comet-Deflecting-Mode&quot; is one of the few charm names that could actually be improved by swapping out the noun for &quot;Prana&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-12-2014, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T17:31:21-07:00","id":111835,"title":"","content":"If you didn't tell me it's a Dragon Blooded charm, I'd have assumed it's alchemical, no kidding. <i>Comet-Deflecting-Mode</i>, really? Did they run out of fortune cookies or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T18:15:09-07:00","id":111848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111689#post111689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I now see that the errata got that and you're acting like that's what it said in Graceful Wicked Masques. Also PCDM is now 8m 1wp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, yes, I'm generally talking about charms in the context of how they existed in the present, not how they exist in the past. PCDM is more expensive, but will *always* defend you from a mortal. Vs a heroic Mortal, the Raksha is boned if he's relying on Bastion.<br /> <br /> Edit: Which, I mean, the Raksha *should* be, because Bastion is an indefinite effect, and long perfect defenses are bad for the game.<br /> <br /> (That said, PCDM *is* too expensive. Unlike say, Awareness, most supernatural beings *do* have charms to enhance attacks, so a defense that fails vs magic is much less valuable than say, stealth that fails vs magic. As pointed out above, this is bad copy pasta from 1e where excellencies were not a thing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":782,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","user":"Lafing Cat","date":". 04-12-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T18:17:17-07:00","id":111851,"title":"","content":"Hey, what's wrong with Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode? It's a perfectly-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although this Charm is costly, it is still prized by Dragon-Blooded soldiers, as it is as close as mere Terrestrial Exalted can come to a perfect melee defense. </div> </div> </div>Sweet merciful Buddha, what the fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T18:24:32-07:00","id":111853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111848#post111848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um, yes, I'm generally talking about charms in the context of how they existed in the present, not how they exist in the past. PCDM is more expensive, but will *always* defend you from a mortal. Vs a heroic Mortal, the Raksha is boned if he's relying on Bastion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The *immunity* granted by Bastion of the Sword is pierced by stunts.<br /> <br /> The +2 to +5 DV, however, is not. Which is what makes this Charm such a cornerstone of the &quot;ridiculous DV cheese&quot; raksha build!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-12T18:31:13-07:00","id":111856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111853#post111853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The *immunity* granted by Bastion of the Sword is pierced by stunts.<br /> <br /> The +2 to +5 DV, however, is not. Which is what makes this Charm such a cornerstone of the &quot;ridiculous DV cheese&quot; raksha build!</div> </div> </div> </div>DV caps. DV boosters are thus fungible, and it doesn't really matter if you're getting it from Bastion or from something else. (That said, yes, Raksha DVs are way too high, but they'd have that even without Bastion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T14:56:12-07:00","id":112253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111851#post111851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, what's wrong with Portentous Comet-Deflecting Mode? It's a perfectly- Sweet merciful Buddha, what the fuck.</div> </div> </div> </div> It blocks everything but an Unblockable attack now. It's a perfect defense whose flaw of Invulnerableity is that it cannot protect from the Unblockable. Same with the dragon bloods perfect dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T15:19:19-07:00","id":112268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112253#post112253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It blocks everything but an Unblockable attack now. It's a perfect defense whose flaw of Invulnerableity is that it cannot protect from the Unblockable. Same with the dragon bloods perfect dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, this isn't true. While text in the errata supersedes contradictory text in the original material, it doesn't replace the original charm in its entirety unless it says <i>&quot;Replace the text of this Charm with the following:</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So PCDM, post-errata, now is an 8m, 1wp perfect parry that still requires you to succeed on a Dex + Melee roll, fails against sorcerous or Charm-enhanced attacks, and cannot block AoE or the unblockable.<br /> <br /> Having removed the ability to block mundane unblockables with it, I'm... not sure why you'd <i>ever</i> use this Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T17:12:21-07:00","id":112328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112268#post112268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this isn't true. While text in the errata supersedes contradictory text in the original material, it doesn't replace the original charm in its entirety unless it says <i>&quot;Replace the text of this Charm with the following:</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So PCDM, post-errata, now is an 8m, 1wp perfect parry that still requires you to succeed on a Dex + Melee roll, fails against sorcerous or Charm-enhanced attacks, and cannot block AoE or the unblockable.<br /> <br /> Having removed the ability to block mundane unblockables with it, I'm... not sure why you'd <i>ever</i> use this Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conflagration of Warding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T17:56:41-07:00","id":112350,"title":"","content":"How is a mundane attack even unblockable? I don't think I've ever seen a unblockable mundane attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T18:13:29-07:00","id":112353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112350#post112350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is a mundane attack even unblockable? I don't think I've ever seen a unblockable mundane attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is likely that &quot;attacks&quot; from forces of nature such as avalanches and tornadoes can often be considered unblockable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T18:43:50-07:00","id":112363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112350#post112350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is a mundane attack even unblockable? I don't think I've ever seen a unblockable mundane attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>A surprise attack is a mundane unblockable attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T22:09:12-07:00","id":112422,"title":"","content":"I think powers that fail against magic are fine in a few specific situations -- generally, abilities with broad applicability where the things they're likely to go up against are correspondingly narrow, such as disguise or tracking charms.<br /> <br /> Here's why: Broad applicability allows those charms to still be useful even against people who can counter them, because they can be applied indirectly - eg. you can simply avoid the guy who can see through your disguise, which I think is a valid part of playing a master of disguise; and your talent at disguise will help you avoid them by letting you take other routes.<br /> <br /> This means you can define a useful charm entirely based around those weaknesses, as long as you keep them in mind when considering the charm's intended use. The Jedi mind-trick, for instance, is basically described as &quot;influence the weak of will.&quot; This probably means that any sort of firm resistance is going to stop it -- it won't work on Jabba the Hutt, and it certainly won't work on Darth Vader. But it's still an incredibly valuable power to have -- even if you can't use it against Dace personally, you <i>can</i> use it to slip past his guards and wait in ambush in his tent.<br /> <br /> The problem is that previous editions have sometimes just slapped fails-vs-magic on charms carelessly or in places where it just felt like a gaping weakness (rather than a Jedi Mind Trick-style &quot;this charm isn't intended to be used directly against your main opponent anyway&quot; sort of thematic.) Having that limitation on Force Push or something else that <i>feels</i> like it's supposed to be a central part of your arsenal is not going to be fun at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-14-2014, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T22:13:36-07:00","id":112424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112350#post112350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is a mundane attack even unblockable? I don't think I've ever seen a unblockable mundane attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giant boulder falling from the sky. House falling on you. Giant behemoths. That kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T23:38:05-07:00","id":112451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is by no means limited to DBs, it's *extraordinarily* common. I'm pretty sure every single splat (and all of the NPC types) has some magic that only works vs (equal or) lower essence targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, now that you quote me on it, I don't know why I said that. I mean, I know that a lot of effects work like that. I think I may have been thinking of something else, but I can't remember the point. Oh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lafing Cat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That said, yes, Raksha DVs are way too high...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Naaaah. Their magic isn't as potent in Creation, so them having just blatantly high stats I think is really awesome. Plus, mixed with their low Essence pools, it's a great way to model their boosted DV's that Charms would otherwise give them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","user":"Arteliex","date":". 04-14-2014, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T00:43:14-07:00","id":112468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112422#post112422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having that limitation on Force Push or something else that <i>feels</i> like it's supposed to be a central part of your arsenal is not going to be fun at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm pretty confident that, at least in the movies, Force Push is rarely, if ever, used against the main antagonist (or even Force users in general). Unless they're already severely weakened, at least.<br /> Most of the time, it's used to throw objects at enemies and sometimes to push mooks (usually droids) around. <br /> Force Lightning would be a better example. <br /> <br /> I do agree with your point, though, just not with your example =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T02:39:05-07:00","id":112507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112424#post112424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Giant boulder falling from the sky. House falling on you. Giant behemoths. That kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should those things be unblockable? I can understand unexpected attacks to be unblockable, but you can (try) to block those things. They're just large projectiles with a AOE travelling at a normal speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T03:58:13-07:00","id":112522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112507#post112507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should those things be unblockable? I can understand unexpected attacks to be unblockable, but you can (try) to block those things. They're just large projectiles with a AOE travelling at a normal speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, here it comes down to letting go of the system abstractions that says &quot;hey, that's just a projectile&quot; and realise that it's a projectile twenty times your size and moving with terrifying momentum. Absent magic (which is what we're talking about here), a single warrior isn't going to block that. Hell, a single warrior isn't going to dodge that, unless the &quot;dodge&quot; means &quot;start running the moment you see it&quot;, which is... more in Athletics, really. Exalts get to ignore stuff like that to a large extent, but mortals are still very much affected by it.<br /> <br /> But if you want mechanics, there is in fact a valid reason to make such phenomena unblockable. That reason is that otherwise, you'd have to calculate an attack dice pool for that falling boulder. It's just much more convenient to say that, without magic, you just can't block that thing. It's also very reasonable to our brains, since that is in fact how it works.<br /> <br /> Edit: If my hunch is right, I think 3e is going to utilize much more of this context sensitive interpretation of the rules than 2e did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 04-14-2014, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T05:41:36-07:00","id":112567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112522#post112522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here it comes down to letting go of the system abstractions that says &quot;hey, that's just a projectile&quot; and realise that it's a projectile twenty times your size and moving with terrifying momentum. Absent magic (which is what we're talking about here), a single warrior isn't going to block that. Hell, a single warrior isn't going to dodge that, unless the &quot;dodge&quot; means &quot;start running the moment you see it&quot;, which is... more in Athletics, really. Exalts get to ignore stuff like that to a large extent, but mortals are still very much affected by it.<br /> <br /> But if you want mechanics, there is in fact a valid reason to make such phenomena unblockable. That reason is that otherwise, you'd have to calculate an attack dice pool for that falling boulder. It's just much more convenient to say that, without magic, you just can't block that thing. It's also very reasonable to our brains, since that is in fact how it works.<br /> <br /> Edit: If my hunch is right, I think 3e is going to utilize much more of this context sensitive interpretation of the rules than 2e did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd join you in that opinion, but my players do use houses/rocks/etc. falling from outer space way too often. I therefore ruled it would be an attack with an attack pool of (fall height) dice and raw damge equal to their (mass / 100kg). This is most similar to Heaven Thunder Hammer, the only true mechanic that can model things without limited velocity.<br /> Therefore a parry DV of 15 or more has the chance of parrying the object, if it only falls from less than 45 yards.<br /> <br /> I already lost 3 BBEG to things comparable to meteors being dropped on them by my players. And in those cases they managed to make it a surprise attack. If I'd just make it unblockable they would use 10-15 of those rocks to first siphon all motes from their target and then kill it. But I do prefer my players not oneshot'ing the Mask of Winters without a plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> And because I always rule the same thing the same way Terrestrials can use their Perfect Parry against such a projectile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T07:38:33-07:00","id":112625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112422#post112422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think powers that fail against magic are fine in a few specific situations -- generally, abilities with broad applicability where the things they're likely to go up against are correspondingly narrow, such as disguise or tracking charms.<br /> <br /> Here's why: Broad applicability allows those charms to still be useful even against people who can counter them, because they can be applied indirectly - eg. you can simply avoid the guy who can see through your disguise, which I think is a valid part of playing a master of disguise; and your talent at disguise will help you avoid them by letting you take other routes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's better if the master of disguise avoids the guy because it's <i>risky</i>, not because it's a guaranteed failure. That gives you more tension: Do you attempt to move about indirectly, or do you just cross your fingers, roll the dice, and see if the disguise holds up? Plus, the &quot;My powers are useless here!&quot; scenario means that it's entirely possible your powers <i>will</i> end up being useless. If your disguise powers fail against, say, royalty, and you want to fool the Queen of England, then your &quot;master of disguise&quot; won't be able to apply his skills at all. If you're disguised as some foreign dignitary, and suddenly the Queen shows up and wants to meet you, you're going to be in trouble. If the Queen is simply really good at seeing through disguises, then you can say &quot;I may be a master of disguise, but can I really fool the Queen?&quot;, weigh the risks, and choose whether you want to abandon the scheme or take the chance. That's far different from saying &quot;Whelp, I can't fool the Queen; might as well give up right now.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Jedi Mind Trick is a poor example to use because it's a binary pass/fail that instantly ends the encounter if successful. If Luke could simply wave his hand and say &quot;You don't want to be on the Dark Side anymore; you want to let go of your hate,&quot; there wouldn't be any story. Hopefully, 3e won't have as many of those &quot;save-or-die&quot; type effects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Note that I'm not going into my <i>other</i> objection to &quot;fails against magic,&quot; which is that magic in Creation is integrated into the very fabric of existence, and therefore should be treated as part of that world's physics rather than as an alien set of rules imposed on mundane reality.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112468#post112468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm pretty confident that, at least in the movies, Force Push is rarely, if ever, used against the main antagonist (or even Force users in general). Unless they're already severely weakened, at least.<br /> Most of the time, it's used to throw objects at enemies and sometimes to push mooks (usually droids) around.<br /> Force Lightning would be a better example.<br /> <br /> I do agree with your point, though, just not with your example =P</div> </div> </div> </div>Force Push gets used against Jedi and Sith. It's not as effective, because Jedi have countermeasures and can recover more easily from being knocked over, but it still happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T08:34:46-07:00","id":112665,"title":"","content":"Powers that fail against magic should generally be a long-duration first line of defense, or else they should be dirt cheap. I have no objection to them under those circumstances!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T19:03:57-07:00","id":113748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=112625#post112625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's better if the master of disguise avoids the guy because it's <i>risky</i>, not because it's a guaranteed failure. That gives you more tension: Do you attempt to move about indirectly, or do you just cross your fingers, roll the dice, and see if the disguise holds up? Plus, the &quot;My powers are useless here!&quot; scenario means that it's entirely possible your powers <i>will</i> end up being useless. If your disguise powers fail against, say, royalty, and you want to fool the Queen of England, then your &quot;master of disguise&quot; won't be able to apply his skills at all. If you're disguised as some foreign dignitary, and suddenly the Queen shows up and wants to meet you, you're going to be in trouble. If the Queen is simply really good at seeing through disguises, then you can say &quot;I may be a master of disguise, but can I really fool the Queen?&quot;, weigh the risks, and choose whether you want to abandon the scheme or take the chance. That's far different from saying &quot;Whelp, I can't fool the Queen; might as well give up right now.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not true. Your disguise powers are still useful to have even if you can't use them to fool the queen -- for example, you can use them to sneak past her guards and get close to her.<br /> <br /> If your response to a limitation your power is &quot;well I can't use this power as a club to brute-force past absolutely everything by using it directly on everyone, so it's sometimes useless and I suck!&quot;, the issue is just in your head. Your disguses are absolutely still useful -- <i>even against royalty</i> -- even if every royal on the planet can see through them instantly with no roll. It is a weakness you have to plan around, which makes for interesting storytelling. Sure, it does mean that your powers will not be 100% applicable in every situation... but no power is. Your disguise-that-fails-vs-royalty charm won't help you directly sneak past a royal's line of vision, but it won't help you make a salad, either; neither of those are part of its function. It is still broadly useful, <i>even against royalty</i>, if you plan ahead and take its limitations into account.<br /> <br /> That's my point. Some powers are designed in a way that makes it both thematically and mechanically useful to say that it doesn't work on everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Jedi Mind Trick is a poor example to use because it's a binary pass/fail that instantly ends the encounter if successful. If Luke could simply wave his hand and say &quot;You don't want to be on the Dark Side anymore; you want to let go of your hate,&quot; there wouldn't be any story. Hopefully, 3e won't have as many of those &quot;save-or-die&quot; type effects. </div> </div> </div>Disguises are often also a binary pass-fail that instantly ends (or bypasses) an encounter if successful. That's why (sometimes, when you have a situation where you don't feel the disguise should be applicable) you can design it to say &quot;your disguise flatly does not function against this guy&quot;; it can be preferable to force players to use their powers in a specific way (working around their limitations and therefore playing out interesting plans) rather than to have it just boil down to a roll of the dice.<br /> <br /> But more generally, consider the problem with &quot;save-or-die&quot;; they turn things into just one die roll. A die roll, on its own divorced of any other context, is often a boring way to handle things. That's why, if you're going to have Jedi mind trick in the setting, it's often better to say &quot;it just doesn't work on these people&quot; rather than allowing a roll -- you don't want people trying to target it at Vader <i>at all</i>, because nothing good is going to come of that. Sometimes it is better to say, upfront, &quot;this charm will not work on rival Jedi&quot; rather than allowing a roll.<br /> <br /> Not always! It has to be done carefully. But the sense I'm getting from your objections is that you don't like the idea of your charms having failure states built into them because it makes you feel weak, rather than because of any mechanical consideration. I don't feel that that's valid -- some charms just aren't meant for certain usages; if you have a power that lets you easily sneak past or command commoners because you are the Exigent of Royalty, it will fail against royals and that's that, and that's a totally cool way for it to work. It has to be considered carefully in the context of the charm's intended use, but I don't see why every charm you have has to give you a chance of successfully using it on Darth Vader in order to be useful.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, note that this ties into the themes of different sorts of characters. Solar charms tend to have few failure states because, in general, Solars are about brute force -- Hypnotic Tongue Technique <i>does</i> work on Vader, because as a Solar who focuses on Presence, your default mode of operation is to apply overwhelming Presence force against your opponent until they crack, whatever that means or requires. (Conversely, though, Solar charms tend to not be as specifically focused on &quot;punching downwards&quot; as other Exalted; Hypnotic Tongue Technique works on mortals, but is priced as a charm that works on anyone.)<br /> <br /> Not everyone else works the same way. Jedis are (in this respect) a bit more like Sidereal or Infernal trees -- you start out with your Jedi Mind Trick intended for reliable use against the weak-willed, then instead of developing into super-presence, the same tree might lead to Force Push or lightsaber combat. In that context it's fine for Jedi Mind Trick to lack the overwhelming force needed to give it a shot against a powerful opponent, because the structure of your charmset is more based around eg. using it to sneak past the guards and then using your lightsaber skills, acrobatics, and telekinesis to murder their boss, rather than using mind control as a universal sledgehammer for absolutely everything the way the focused Solar would.<br /> <br /> Also, important! You said that you felt that you'd prefer if the &quot;master of disguise&quot; had a chance to sneak past anyone, no matter how powerful they are. But that's not how everyone's powers work -- different charmsets have different themes. Master of disguise is the charm-thematic behind Solar Larceny, say, so again, it makes sense for their disguise charm to work against everyone. But if you're playing that Exigent of Royalty with a charm that says &quot;mere commoners cannot obstruct me&quot;, it makes much more sense for your charm to fail against the queen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-15-2014, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:15:38-07:00","id":113768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=113748#post113748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not always! It has to be done carefully. <b>But the sense I'm getting from your objections is that you don't like the idea of your charms having failure states built into them because it makes you feel weak, rather than because of any mechanical consideration. I don't feel that that's valid</b> -- some charms just aren't meant for certain usages; if you have a power that lets you easily sneak past or command commoners because you are the Exigent of Royalty, it will fail against royals and that's that, and that's a totally cool way for it to work. It has to be considered carefully in the context of the charm's intended use, but I don't see why every charm you have has to give you a chance of successfully using it on Darth Vader in order to be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... totally valid to feel that way about an effect. You can argue that the effect being that way is justified up and down, but arguing that objecting to the result regardless of justification is invalid is... well, weird at best, and dismissive of other people desiring certain playstyles when taken less charitably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T20:53:59-07:00","id":113792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=113768#post113768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>But the sense I'm getting from your objections is that you don't like the idea of your charms having failure states built into them because it makes you feel weak, rather than because of any mechanical consideration. I don't feel that that's valid</b> </div> </div> </div>It's... totally valid to feel that way about an effect. You can argue that the effect being that way is justified up and down, but arguing that objecting to the result regardless of justification is invalid is... well, weird at best, and dismissive of other people desiring certain playstyles when taken less charitably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Not every charmset is going to support every playstyle. Some charmsets (like the Solar one) are going to have few inherent failure states in their charms, so if you prefer a playstyle where your charms are broadly-applicable and capable of brute-forcing almost any situation where they can be remotely construed as applicable, play a type of Exalted like that.<br /> <br /> But there are other playstyles which require different sorts of designs, including charms that will have unusual built-in failure states to fit unusual thematics, or charms which aren't designed to be used directly against hard targets. To me, it seems like <i>you</i> are the one who is being dismissive of other playstyles -- you're saying &quot;I don't want charms like this to exist, because they make me feel weak and therefore should not exist anywhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nobody's forcing you to play a Dragon-Blooded! But within the DB paradigm (as well as several other Exalted), it's entirely valid to have a charm that is designed for utility support against weaker targets and not intended to be used against &quot;hard&quot; opposition. The fact that this has sometimes been done badly doesn't mean that it's always invalid.<br /> <br /> If you don't like that kind of charm... don't take it. Play a kind of Exalted with fewer or more &quot;natural&quot;-feeling limitations, or focus on other charms instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T21:08:33-07:00","id":113803,"title":"","content":"Just let all my fail-again-magic disguise/tracking/hiding charms be all one-mote and I will be happy, oh, and I can add my Essence + Breeding in automatic successes too, 'cause I ain't gonna pay 10m,1wp only to be defeated by an Excellency ( \uff65\u0e34\u0437\uff65\u0e34)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-16-2014, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T22:44:41-07:00","id":113862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=113792#post113792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Not every charmset is going to support every playstyle. Some charmsets (like the Solar one) are going to have few inherent failure states in their charms, so if you prefer a playstyle where your charms are broadly-applicable and capable of brute-forcing almost any situation where they can be remotely construed as applicable, play a type of Exalted like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because someone saying &quot;I don't like this&quot; is not a statement it's reasonable to call invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T02:09:13-07:00","id":113928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>notthepenguins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=113862#post113862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because someone saying &quot;I don't like this&quot; is not a statement it's reasonable to call invalid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Invalid as a critique of the mechanics. Aquillion can't comment on the validity of your tastes and opinions, only on the validity of the arguments you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T02:54:53-07:00","id":113939,"title":"","content":"Errata breathed a little life into a lot of the DB set by reducing some of the limitations. The set that still really suffers is Investigation, which still flatly fails against Celestial Exalts for most of its Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:18:13-07:00","id":114000,"title":"","content":"There's nothing <i>inherently</i> wrong against fail vs. magic.<br /> That's actually why I brought up Bastion of Self before we went on that merry tangent. The Fair Folk have a permanent charm that says &quot;I'm immune to extras&quot; in a white room fight with Exalts it doesn't matter, but it makes a statement about the Raksha's narrative significance and the role they play that's a lot more flattering than what PCDM says about Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:30:20-07:00","id":114181,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I should clarify. I'm not talking about raw power per se, I'm talking about giving the player options. Saying &quot;Your disguise automatically fails against the Queen&quot; forces the player to use disguises indirectly and avoid the Queen whenever possible. Saying &quot;The Queen knows this guy really well, and need I remind you that she used to be a mere Baroness with a lot of ambition and a scheming intellect?&quot; has much the same result, but you've still got the <i>option</i> to try. It will probably turn out badly for you, but if you're crazy or desperate enough to take the risk, a legitimate &quot;You gave it your best, but it wasn't enough&quot; is better than &quot;lol, nope.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1369-mewtarthio","name":"Mewtarthio","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T16:51:33-07:00","id":114416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mewtarthio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=114181#post114181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I should clarify. I'm not talking about raw power per se, I'm talking about giving the player options. Saying &quot;Your disguise automatically fails against the Queen&quot; forces the player to use disguises indirectly and avoid the Queen whenever possible. Saying &quot;The Queen knows this guy really well, and need I remind you that she used to be a mere Baroness with a lot of ambition and a scheming intellect?&quot; has much the same result, but you've still got the <i>option</i> to try. It will probably turn out badly for you, but if you're crazy or desperate enough to take the risk, a legitimate &quot;You gave it your best, but it wasn't enough&quot; is better than &quot;lol, nope.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>that is also what baffles me, in that PCDM has a cost equal to an effect that can beat charm enhanced attacks. The Original cost was better reflective of it's abilities than the new errated version, as most Dragonbloods who have sufficient melee skill to take this, are not concerned about mortals they are probably fighting elementals, gods, demons, and anathema. In short they need a version that says &quot;blocks any attack so long as it isn't unblockable, this limit plus the roll to activate count as the flaw of invulnerability&quot; I was discussing with another that it seems that the dragon blooded could never have pulled of the usurpation outside of narrative space because their charms leave them no way to defeat established solar. The only way I could see it happening is if there were solar's who believed in the bronze faction's idea and agreed to go along with it in exchange for a peaceful death when their time came.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T19:44:15-07:00","id":114500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/111399-dragon-blooded-vs-magic?p=111522#post111522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effects of Dragon-Blooded vs Celestial Magic... or Dragon-Blooded vs higher-Essence magic... I thought was pretty lame. I don't find it interesting inside the setting, and as a player I don't find the extra challenge fun when presented in that manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second type i'm a little less bothered with, but either way i have replaced both types of weakness with a Iron Skin Concentration-esque &quot;Roll (his Skill + Essence) against a difficulty equal to the opponent\u2019s Essence. On a success, the Charm works normally but becomes Obvious (if not so already)&quot; or something along those lines. Makes things a bit more convoluted, but can be fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: i use a little personal system, based in the logic of wyld resistance (page 284 of 2e core) to balance between tweaked/made up charms while maintaning the power level gap. Essence is the core of all charms divine, demonic or elemental, but the exalts' essence reflect the might of something greater than themselves. Dragon-Blooded add one die to their pool, Sidereal &amp; Lunars add two dice, and Solars and their twisted variants add three.*<br /> <br /> So it will mean, for example, that an Ess 2 solar charm (like many of their perfects) will be somewhat equivalent to an Ess 3 sidereal or lunar charm (ditto), Ess 4 terrestrial charms (where one may find some perfect-esque effects) and a Ess 5 spirit charm (where one finds their generic perfect too). This sort of frame of reference has been most useful when it comes to balancing charms inspired by systems from other exalts, balancing NPCs or better customizing a spirit and its charms (or balancing the MA charms from Scroll of the Monk).<br /> <br /> To this i have added a little caveat: Essence 8+ deities add one to their Ess when defining charm power (like terrestrials), Essence 10 deities add 2 (like celestials). These bonus reflect on any charms that emanate of their power, such as those of any descendants or hypothetical chosen.<br /> <br /> And yes, i admit such &quot;hypothetical chosen&quot; and their making were the actual motive behind the caveat - and whole little system - all along. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The whole idea of such a system came from Infernals &amp; the Glories series and an understanding of their charmsets/panoplies as the ultimate expression/customization/extrapolation of spirit charms.<br /> <br /> In case you are asking themselves how solars +3 fits into this, it reflects the UCS keyword/purview/specialty of perfection/surpassing others bumping up an Essence 10 deity's +2. We use that kind of things to fudge the system balance dynamic here and there and to explain/reflect some spirits having charms 1-2 levels higher than their Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Me and my group are so far undecided about where in the scale we should put alchemicals (what will certainly change fast the moment we actually play them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-17-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}